cted by Ralph Hewins in the course of researching and writing the biography <emph render=\\\"italic\\\">The Richest American: J. Paul Getty</emph> (1960). The material dates from around the 1890s to 1973 and includes correspondence that discusses Hewins\' writings about Getty, a number of unpublished manuscripts, personal photographs given to Hewins by Mr. Getty, and other related photographs, clippings, and ephemera belonging to Hewins.\"],\"type\":\"abstract\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_bf97d6aaa832b77b0416dc9153b5d72a\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1380,1,19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"<emph render=\\\"italic\\\">The following materials are offered as possible sources of further information on the people, programs, and subjects covered by the records. The listing is not exhaustive. </emph> \\n\\n<emph render=\\\"bold\\\">Publications</emph> \\n\\n<bibref><persname>Hewins, Ralph. </persname><title><emph render=\\\"italic\\\">The Richest American: J. Paul Getty.</emph></title> New York: Dutton, 1960. </bibref>\\n\\n<emph render=\\\"bold\\\">Archival Materials</emph> \\n\\n<repository><emph render=\\\"bold\\\">Getty Institutional Archives</emph> </repository> \\n\\n<archref>Art and Real Estate Holding Companies Records, 1939-1982 and undated, J. Paul Getty. The Getty Research Institute (IA20011).</archref>\\n\\n<archref>J. Paul Getty and the Ashby Sisters Papers, 1926-1992 and undated. The Getty Research Institute (IA20013).</archref>\\n\\n<archref>J. Paul Getty Family Papers, circa 1880s-1989 and undated. The Getty Research Institute (IA20009).</archref>\\n\\n<archref>J. Paul Getty Diaries, 1938-1946, 1948-1976. The Getty Research Institute (IA40009).</archref>\",\"subnote_guid\":\"6820552f7657dc52808cdcf071536a08\"}],\"type\":\"relatedmaterial\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_29e08b7caa7ac5ca030ee96eb65a2e9c\",\"label\":\"Related Materials Note\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1381,1,19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"In 2005 Sue Luftschein rehoused the materials and created this finding aid based, in part, on the preliminary inventory. In 2010 Cyndi Shein arranged and described the photographs, and revised the finding aid.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"25f1bb1e2fd281d2f02dc28831629e4c\"}],\"type\":\"processinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_85448d417f88b8f208662d4d218ed425\",\"label\":\"Processing History\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1382,1,19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The collection was donated to the Getty by Ralph Hewins in 1984 and subsequently assigned accession number 1986.IA.10.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"2b91cec17334d16783ff6ee01d700ca6\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_79cfefcbf107554938884843a83d70e2\",\"label\":\"Acquisition Information\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1383,1,19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"[Cite the item and series (as appropriate)], Collected Papers for Biography of J. Paul Getty, circa 1890s-1973, 1984 and undated, Ralph Hewins. The Getty Research Institute (IA20012).\\n\\n http://hdl.handle.net/10020/cifaia20012\",\"subnote_guid\":\"ab70dbe8f70b3b545b90082660794f7c\"}],\"type\":\"prefercite\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_4d7c1b12904df47a7097a9be605353eb\",\"label\":\"Preferred Citation\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1384,1,19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Contact <extref actuate=\\\"onrequest\\\" href=\\\"http://hdl.handle.net/10020/rights_repro\\\" show=\\\"new\\\"> Rights and Reproductions </extref> at the Getty Research Institute for copyright information and permission to publish.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"b73e4a4faca2918b7cbde713b08f6f3b\"}],\"type\":\"userestrict\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_9c5dc1a3dd3bcf37574839e8679fcded\",\"label\":\"Restrictions on Use\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1385,1,19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The records described in accession 1986.IA.10 are available for use by qualified researchers. \\n\\nThe following types of records are permanently closed: records containing personal information, records that compromise security or operations, legal communications, legal work product, and records related to donors. The J. Paul Getty Trust reserves the right to restrict access to any records held by the Institutional Archives.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"d4dc158154e418947159f13ac802896f\"}],\"type\":\"accessrestrict\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_36856a3ef0b3866dcd72e60e1b84b72b\",\"label\":\"Restrictions on Access\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1386,1,19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The collection comprises material created or collected by Ralph Hewins in the course of researching and writing the biography <emph render=\\\"italic\\\">The Richest American: J. Paul Getty</emph> (1960). The material dates from around the 1890s to 1973 and 1984 and includes correspondence that discusses Hewins\' writings about Getty, a number of unpublished manuscripts, personal photographs given to Hewins by Mr. Getty, and other related photographs, clippings, and ephemera belonging to Hewins. The collection has two main strengths: the unpublished material and the photographs.\\n\\nThe papers include a substantial body of correspondence between Hewins and Getty, as well as scattered letters received from Allene Ashby, Penelope Kitson and other Getty family members and associates. The manuscripts comprise Hewins\' published and unpublished material about Getty, probably assembled as a potential update to the 1960 biography. These writings are mainly anecdotal in nature; some relate to Getty\'s friendships and others to his business or recreational activities. A large file of photocopied international clippings chronicle Getty\'s press coverage through the fifties, sixties and seventies, many of these concerning the kidnapping of Getty\'s grandson.\\n\\nThe photographic prints and negatives contain over 200 unique images, ranging from approximately the 1890s to the late 1960s, collected by Ralph Hewins. The images include an array of professional photographs and informal snapshots of Getty, his wives, children, friends, associates, businesses, properties, projects, and residences. Some of the images were published in Hewins\' book.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"a0dd63341b8845ec7441483331002888\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_508c319f619201d55450d651833dbb8e\",\"label\":\"Scope and Content of Collection\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1387,1,19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"These records are organized in three series: \\n\\n<ref audience=\\\"external\\\" target=\\\"ref25\\\">Series I. Correspondence, 1957-1971, undated; </ref> \\n\\n<ref audience=\\\"external\\\" target=\\\"ref33\\\">Series II. Manuscripts and background information, 1960-1973, 1984, undated; </ref> \\n\\n<ref audience=\\\"external\\\" target=\\\"ref71\\\">Series III. Photographs, circa 1890s-1960s.</ref>\",\"subnote_guid\":\"bdfe0786b245bb804344f67e27029826\"}],\"type\":\"arrangement\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_8f1a8869bcb6480e8b9a8a0d207cc785\",\"label\":\"Arrangement\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1388,1,19,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Ralph Hewins (d. 1984) was a professional journalist largely concerned with the very wealthy. He was the author of <emph render=\\\"italic\\\">The Richest American: J. Paul Getty</emph> (1960). Hewins became a personal friend of Mr. Getty during the years he spent researching and writing Getty\'s biography.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"727f566535644e48ed73d9b819415042\"}],\"type\":\"bioghist\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_3c4ef7e955cde8915605d4e5f1e6bb56\",\"label\":\"Biography\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1389,1,NULL,1638,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"These records are arranged in general chronological order.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"006ff3d12b898634e61c5fabe0c279a1\"}],\"type\":\"arrangement\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_377e7c7e6339b5265d9c5d75e10b3c74\",\"label\":\"Arrangement\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1390,1,NULL,1638,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Records consist of correspondence, primarily to and from Ralph Hewins, a biographer and acquaintance of J. Paul Getty, 1957-1971 and undated. This correspondence largely relates to Hewins\' writings on Getty, and includes correspondence with Getty and other individuals, including Maxwell Balfour, president of Getty\'s Spartan Aircraft Company. The letters discuss the publication of Hewins\' 1960 biography of Getty, <emph render=\\\"italic\\\">The Richest American</emph>, as well as personal events in Hewins\' life related to his work on the biography.\\n\\nSee also Series III. Photographs, for related photographs.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"8e412434a443a810fb7eeb32821d93b0\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_4c6f44468534d55f17cbc77bab385818\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents note\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1391,1,NULL,1639,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"These records are generally arranged in the order of accession. The larger manuscripts have been grouped together.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"7de94b9a1d9911b9a4123cc4e267cbbc\"}],\"type\":\"arrangement\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_0dfae7e17329ffc5364ff0ae31cf8458\",\"label\":\"Arrangement\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1392,1,NULL,1639,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Records consist of typescript manuscripts, clippings, ephemera, and photographs, 1960-1973, 1984, and undated, written and collected by Ralph Hewins about J. Paul Getty and comprising Hewins\' published and unpublished material about Getty. Some of the material seems to have been assembled as an update to his book, <emph render=\\\"italic\\\">The Richest American: J. Paul Getty</emph> (New York: 1960). The manuscripts are a set of short articles and two versions of the manuscript for <emph render=\\\"italic\\\">The Zillionaire: Getty at 80</emph> (unpublished); these contain Hewins\' edits. The short works are anecdotal in nature; some relate to Getty\'s friendships and others to his business or recreational activities. The ephemera consists of cards, invitations and announcements relating to Getty and his companies.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"fbabf90b8dcd845d4edf7c0ffd041e54\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_f46cdf17e229e2c09afd2c94d3f70fce\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents note\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1393,1,NULL,1640,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The photographs have been roughly arranged by subject. Within each subject the images are arranged numerically accoring to the creator\'s original numbering system (some prints have numbers written in pencil on the verso). Some of the photographic prints are accompanied by negatives, which are housed in neighboring sleeves.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"d637aaf4ecd6a28706a1357a9c877e33\"}],\"type\":\"arrangement\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_cefe2742949300b6162b37243d468695\",\"label\":\"Arrangement\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1394,1,NULL,1640,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Materials consist of over 200 photographic prints and negatives, ranging from around the 1890s to the late 1960s, collected by Ralph Hewins, depicting J. Paul Getty, family, friends, business associates, properties, and a reception for Hewins\' book <emph render=\\\"italic\\\">The Richest American: J. Paul Getty</emph> (1960). The records also include photocopies of all photographs. Some of the photographs were published in Hewins\' book. The vast majority of the photographs are black-and-white.\\n\\nSee also Series I. Correspondence, for related items.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"521a57f4a1e057b6f8812deb2f75d905\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_0662cafda32b27a69f63c194643e3d44\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents note\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1395,1,NULL,1641,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"[2 files]\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_15ebd3684992dcd5e0060ba4fa97539d\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1396,1,NULL,1642,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"[2 files]\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_b2e918768e44a711373df29e333fdc4a\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1397,1,NULL,1644,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"[4 files]\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_2b38ee26afe8ae5805c25d20c7610737\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1398,1,NULL,1645,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"[4 files]\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_1323daa21358f0e9f0d0ead9e9c99068\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1399,1,NULL,1647,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"[2 files]\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_a42a9e543241372fc670786a3b8d5bfe\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1400,1,NULL,1648,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"[1-2 of 5 files]\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_aa7c0dbf4547a4777e3e5661af5649fb\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1401,1,NULL,1649,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"[3-5 of 5 files]\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_56b5f8a14559cd1188d1fec5522d1dcc\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58','2019-07-26 20:44:58',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1402,1,NULL,1672,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"[5 files]\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_354f923092473bae1c3f87a786b0b34b\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1403,1,NULL,1677,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(approximately 42 images)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_b7f38b75f7b4b2d2f507e1e8ec9f5e6c\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1404,1,NULL,1677,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Material comprises formal portraits and casual snapshots featuring J. Paul Getty, including photographs of him as a child, with family, with a couple of his wives, with friends, with business associates, with his Spartan aircraft staff, with English Queen Elizabeth the Queen Mother, and with his lion cub. Material also includes shots of Getty receiving the Legion of Honor, receiving an honorary academic degree, standing in oil fields, standing on deck the tanker \\\"George F. Getty,\\\" and visiting archaeological sites. All but one of the photos is in black-and-white.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"16600c449d71e3d05efa0baa23bdfdd1\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_86afb0cc199fabf5d04b7ff43463a87e\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1405,1,NULL,1678,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(approximately 23 images)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_31276c896125eadf9a33fcdce906c135\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1406,1,NULL,1678,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Material comprises images of J. Paul Getty\'s parents, George F. Getty I and Sarah C. Getty; sister, Gertrude Lois Getty; wives, Jeannette McDermot, Allene Ashby, Ann Rork, Fini Helmly; children, Eugene Paul Getty II, Gordon Getty, George F. Getty, and Timmy Getty; and young grandchildren, Anne, Caroline, Claire, and J. Paul Getty III. Photos of wife, Teddy are located with the photos of J. Paul Getty. Photos of Ronald Getty are located with Ralph Hewins\' book signing images. Persons listed above may also appear in images of various events listed below. Images are black-and-white except for one hand-tinted photograph of Allene Ashby.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"119f8827858d07e52e88dc4fe92d3048\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_4b3f173b811cffa8fe05f58c1b04803f\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1407,1,NULL,1679,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(12 images)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_cd7b378fd7cf4a19547ab3dcefd68a91\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1408,1,NULL,1679,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Material comprises images of Getty residences: South Kingsley Drive (Los Angeles); Sutton Place (England); exterior of the Getty Ranch House (near Malibu, California) and its zoo; and La Posta Vecchia (Gaeta, Italy).\",\"subnote_guid\":\"c4cb37aab59432f35844b05c47d67bde\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_83835abf23195e9a6d745e0b43f8fdf2\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1409,1,NULL,1680,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(approximately 12 images)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_479a7b70115b005ae4f9b11e0aae42ec\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1410,1,NULL,1680,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Material includes photographs of Ralph Hewins, Penelope Kitson, President Eisenhower, and others.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"25ef94fa8b969dfe34ab5f3af62d00b8\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_39238954fe9e35559dba14e09996825b\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1411,1,NULL,1681,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(3 images)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_98bcaba0278aaaac8a821f58ab7ee371\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1412,1,NULL,1681,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Materials include images of a museum gallery within the Getty Ranch House, the \\\"Ardibil Carpet,\\\" and the \\\"Medalllion and Tree Carpet.\\\"\",\"subnote_guid\":\"1e1c6915bd8caa452a0bafc12c23c824\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_e23b47638b23646974946f3d1f14114b\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1413,1,NULL,1682,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(approximately 20 images)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_3424440485aad51ee53764e8ea7c5115\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1414,1,NULL,1682,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Material includes images of Japanese business associates, an oil tanker, Ralph Hewins, and others.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"c37ac9e5c174b81d779b5e8c5f6a332c\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_d16b85e1ce3d5165a871f3cfe6833e01\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1415,1,NULL,1683,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(7 images)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_17668e7bd1e2281c0b680e39828b7e0b\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1416,1,NULL,1683,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Material includes an aerial view of the Spartan facility, and Spartan mobile home interiors, William F. Humphry, Maxwell W. Balfour, and British Royal Air Force (RAF) student pilots at the Spartan School of Aeronautics. See also images of J. Paul Getty for an additional photograph of Spartan employees.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"4992e1076017a5379244f578a7669342\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_2569ada70b6f4134e4f5a384ea32a370\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1417,1,NULL,1684,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(approximately 82 images)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_41e4924e6b4a2bad8279e452bdf78019\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1418,1,NULL,1684,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Material comprises exterior shots of various Getty buildings and models of buildings; refineries; filling station; interior of the Cotillion Room (Hotel Pierre, NY); aerial view of Hotel Pierre Marques (Alcapulco); and oil tankers, derricks, drilling sites, pipelines, employees and other shots related to the petroleum business.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"df8ec8fca0de2a32f0936495498ad8de\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_d9d5322c7a67ab9a645b22730440af42\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1419,1,NULL,1685,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(26 8 x 10\\\"; 27 3 x 5\\\"; and 2 3 x 5\\\" color)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_9bf4af7c0cfbd20a797601d9ffa07311\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1420,1,NULL,1685,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Materials comprise professional photographs stamped \\\"Hotel Pierre Public Relations, Fifth Ave. &amp; 61st Street, New York, N.Y.\\\" and \\\"Please credit Irwin Dribben, New York\\\" on verso. Photographs feature Ralph Hewins, George F. Getty II, and Gloria Getty.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"4e894ddb1044222ffeac79f1dcd6ddef\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_01193bfd3e44bb7b55d6403f4d5dd4e9\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1421,1,NULL,1686,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"(approximately 18 images)\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_23724847e6ea1e88394b242106e06a0b\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1422,1,NULL,1686,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Material documents a reception held at the J. Paul Getty Museum (galleries and courtyard of the Ranch House) to commemorate the publication of Ralph Hewins\' biography of J. Paul Getty. Material includes images of Ralph Hewins; George F. Getty II and his wife, Gloria Getty; Ronald Getty, and his mother, Fini Helmle; and others.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"3aaf721276e66a139d6c22b1ed47d8a9\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_9b318a1123dd0e8869e9073f937ce843\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','nancye','nancye','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59','2019-07-26 20:44:59',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1930,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,156,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_bioghist\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"who might exist\",\"subnote_guid\":\"a9c2420cc89eb1874346b48204a25214\"},{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_citation\",\"content\":[\"Some dude\"],\"persistent_id\":\"6816b94efb0a74f35afc2c7705bbe77d\",\"subnote_guid\":\"3f8b0a1e808ad1623335e0471d7ce79f\"}],\"persistent_id\":\"34e7bd5f009f000e398215ca15e51ae7\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-24 17:14:39','2019-09-24 17:14:39','2019-09-24 17:14:39',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1941,1,NULL,1852,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The majority of the 136 letters in the series were composed by Benjamin Rush, and letters he wrote to Julia during the 1793 yellow fever epidemic in Philadelphia form a substantial part of the series. Main topics in the letters include Rush family matters, medical treatments for a wide variety of medical issues, American politics, and the country\'s relations with European nations. Other topics include mental illness and its treatment, the medical department in the Continental Army, the impact of epidemics upon commerce internationally, reading habits, parenting, and capital punishment. \\n\\n Among the prominent correspondents who wrote one or more personal or professional letters to Rush or his wife are Abigail Adams, John Quincy Adams, Thomas Jefferson, James Madison, Thomas Paine, and George Washington. Letters from others to Julia Rush seek to continue ties with her and the Rush family, and offer condolences following Benjamin\'s death. Included are several manuscript copies Benjamin Rush made of individual letters he penned.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"7d1dcf24b725d6564360e4354f0e4579\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_1d84af23d3e3d83e72fb78816cf937ac\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1942,1,NULL,1853,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Contains a medical case book and a fragment of an essay or lecture written by Benjamin Rush, along with his travel diary for a trip to meet with the Board of Trustees for Dickinson College in 178[4]. Other materials include Julia Rush\'s devotional journal and exercise book, as well as an undated presentation note written by Richard Rush.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"e361e5643f16618c85df6077124dd1fd\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_da23aa3ec37c766cf0216c96198efc87\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1943,1,NULL,1854,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Includes a few medical statements and receipts, along with two volumes of household accounts maintained by Benjamin Rush, one in conjunction with his wife. Along with general expenses and accounting information, the account books feature the employment records for Rush family staff and servants, often containing comments on the character and notable aspects of the employment history of each employee.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"7bc516c4f54f6a79ab9a3b69828d1f33\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_94643a8dc2d4b81a292c88202a8a517d\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1944,1,NULL,1855,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Present are Benjamin Rush\'s sworn statement regarding a certificate for Dickinson College, a patent for a tract of land Rush purchased in 1795, along with a certificate of attendance Rush signed for one of his students at the College of Philadelphia Medical School.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"0f26be4fd0dbc5bf8b4a352696b33e81\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_d82a8e508d2f7c1384eb9b46c8793d3d\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1945,1,NULL,1856,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"2 pages; 25 cm\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_717e6e77121231544747fdbd5822b743\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1946,1,NULL,1856,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"9d64d1820ca96f012e982b7121443b18\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_e3d4e6ac026b471ef6a81534077bdd0a\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1947,1,NULL,1856,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Adams sends her condolences to Rush, and confides her own concern about her daughter\'s struggles with breast cancer.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"9ef043f89a6710f0c0e77bf232ed7337\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_5c44926032cef7263543010093924178\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44','2019-09-25 01:14:44',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(1948,1,NULL,1857,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"2 pages; 23 cm\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_