r Rush to dine with the ?Washington.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"21e123c6ea1e597732accb8b5d494a81\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_6f19242e08f603bc9ac4d5917f6b5631\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2406,1,NULL,1991,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"3 pages; 23 cm\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_46a64524b4565268139df7dad0940435\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2407,1,NULL,1991,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"bf6fc47e282a00947331f1b08699ba98\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_3ac1f0680fa5519cb0fd6a08f3d49bf1\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2408,1,NULL,1991,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Wayne describes his fever and consumption and their treatment, following his loss of blood \\\"in defence of the rights &amp; liberties of America, \'from her coldest, to her hottest sun.\'\\\"\",\"subnote_guid\":\"8f0ef3a0919dfbaf71daf489d86bf68c\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_5a782a343b23db2212002a9f6e60fa74\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2409,1,NULL,1992,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"23 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_a45a4c59ffb453d5f2b58b6d837abb73\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2410,1,NULL,1992,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The diary records Rush\'s travel, accompanied by a servant and via horses, between the outskirts of Philadelphia and Carlisle, Pennsylvania, for an initial meeting with the trustees of Dickinson College. During the meeting the Trustees selected Dr. Charles Nisbet to serve as the College\'s first president. Rush described the taverns and other travel lodges at which he stopped, along with Tavern staff and other patrons, the quality of the food and drink, along with conversations he witnessed or took part in. Discussion often centered on the topics of the Constitution, paper money, as well as Dickinson College. Rush also described the results of a rapid Spring thaw on the Susquehanna River, the unusually cold weather, the scenery, and the presence whiskey stills in Irish settlements and their impact on their communities.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"5828bca3ee7633095b5699863917806a\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_16c9784312f30f9a01441146f64f7f99\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2411,1,NULL,1992,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"e4bcabc7f9525f30dede73d24e7b7429\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_0fc510c13bbab565bec03a2a58c2e0e1\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2412,1,NULL,1992,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"5-page transcription available\",\"subnote_guid\":\"a0fe53f284e87e11096d28835f5add17\"}],\"type\":\"altformavail\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_78e9daaa7019023fc12e43a8f17dbb3a\",\"label\":\"Existence and Location of Copies\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2413,1,NULL,1993,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"74 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_c76be363ccb3bd16799674e3906634b4\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2414,1,NULL,1993,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"a34dca0bbd610eaddf4bee5b12032927\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_072b51eae28123e8565932f6e1e096c5\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2415,1,NULL,1993,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"In the casebook, Rush provided brief histories for his treatment of about 75 individuals. Entries generally included the year, patient\'s name, presented medical issue, dates of treatment, prescriptions applied, pulses noted, and the progression or resolution of the problem. Rheumatism was the most common complaint, along with dropsy (edema), pneumonia, diarrhea, and mania. Among the other illnesses listed were palsy (paralysis), fever, typhus, epilepsy, consumption, scurvy, hydrothorax, swelled spleen, and hysteria.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"857209fa5be3d797c71824edc22cb412\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_9e36419b9eff8c519091709a75f0febb\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2416,1,NULL,1994,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"222 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_fef8d7befb873261a81c3548298b871e\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2417,1,NULL,1994,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Rush not only detailed her religious thoughts and practiced devotional exercises but also outlined her feelings regarding family matters, especially in regard to her bereavement following her husband\'s death. She requested intersession for family members, such as when her daughters emigrated to England and Canada and their later return, when they suffered serious illnesses, and blessings for the christenings of her grandchildren. She also noted her general physical and mental health as she aged. Entries are irregular, but often annually mark the New Year and her birthday on March 2nd.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"d7c8ab315ca11a621dbca5796f98a79c\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_111b12b49443e042ddd5fa9356ea43e6\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2418,1,NULL,1994,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"a54bb3a5820df6eb412545e9e6bea579\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_ccc184c780ae0c4a95f76f91fa7a9fbc\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2419,1,NULL,1995,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"2-page transcription available.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"eee29c61fdb3ced4b3310497fc1bda33\"}],\"type\":\"altformavail\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_b16bbaf275e2a4346ab7ba9286497c06\",\"label\":\"Existence and Location of Copies\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2420,1,NULL,1995,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Lecture or essay regarding use of cordial remedies and bleeding, a discussion of influenza, along with a 2-page partial report on an autopsy that noted the presence of a tumor in the abdomen.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"dfeb1ad4f98181669f69fdcd1fb964b3\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_f2abec9d0f2042719b76e7eb7e55c419\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2421,1,NULL,1995,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"0968b030609cf3f0d583c78153ca5d41\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_2bf589605f06c5c978dd687c07232296\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55','2019-09-25 01:14:55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2422,1,NULL,1996,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Presentation note for three unnamed items initialed by Richard Rush, son of Bejamin and Julia Stockton Rush.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"c534e42c1bcb4e712e5cc8924b122005\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_0053dfed5bc13ffeee4c14ac6414fd5f\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2423,1,NULL,1996,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"a56853f0ca83ca8fed1f989bfd36281c\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_0358b21ecdc3d38c16528900f8dae910\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2424,1,NULL,1997,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Includes statements and receipts for medicines, advice, consultations, and sundries. In one case, Rush collected a fee on behalf of another physician. Julia Stockton Rush also served as collector, along with her husband. Includes a receipt from Richard Henderson in Leesburg, Va., for payment on the account of Mr. Carter, who had been a patient in Rush\'s care (see Letters series).\",\"subnote_guid\":\"105c0c7f5db58c9c1d275675194757cc\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_2d5e8a4ed5c22211fde63c52e773df7f\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2425,1,NULL,1997,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"af9536d7ec1fff67d8db70c778af8dc9\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_2606f259f35e550d36ee47f534643164\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2426,1,NULL,1998,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"259 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_b94a693ec6dd9288b3fc30089d0486b1\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2427,1,NULL,1998,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Contains primarily Benjamin Rush\'s records of his expenses, including tax and bond payments, rental property fees, classes and dance lessons for family members, as well as money lent or advanced, accounts paid, cash received, and income from boarders. Rush noted the wide variety of areas where his money was spent, from postage and travel, to clothing and shoes, to household provisions and stores, along with medicines purchased. In addition, Rush created accounts for servants when they arrived, and noted their wages and any increased wages, advances, or loans; cloth, clothing, and shoes provided; with occasional notes on their personal and work habits and work history, and when they exited his service or married. Several of the comments have been redacted, along with a few pages of the account book. Finally, Rush made a few brief commonplace notes randomly in the volume, providing a \\\"style sheet\\\" for description of pulses, outlining a few prescriptions for patients, describing the weather, listing inventories of his furniture and linens, recording a few recipes, and in 1783, noting the news of possible peace with England.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"17df979c1696fa8da0775d72565ae229\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_fab942e5a8250b77ef1823c9ee7ddf86\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2428,1,NULL,1998,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"a405cfbf9d4962a3398933839781d6dc\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_fff7d43fbae42c1db84c25ecdf5c4e72\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2429,1,NULL,1999,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"146 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_68ec4e660c6cfe98eddce4bb9aee7dcb\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2430,1,NULL,1999,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Contains primarily accounts for individuals the Rush\'s employed in their household, including various house servants, cooks, coachmen, farmers and gardeners, along with accounts for work completed by washerwomen outside the residence. Individual accounts include the servant\'s name, followed by notes on pay and payments made, as well as any holds on pay, advances, loans, and pay rate increases. They also indicated when an individual was supplied with shoes or clothing, or had time off to visit the country. In addition, for the majority of the individuals, Benjamin continued his habit of adding a descriptive note when the person left their service, stating the reason for the departure, commenting on the quality of that servant\'s work, outlining their personal and work habits (especially their drinking habits), whether they married or not, and their race or ethnic background. Includes an incomplete alphabetical index for servant names. There are a few additional household accounts briefly noted, for wood and an umbrella, as well as two receipts, one for taxes and another (laid-in) for bread.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"c390861d9e024cd5754b0191827fd33c\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_5c96ad6ec2fa68e3ea1b4d4890d74a1d\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2431,1,NULL,1999,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"d7af71a96d2c2139c689f05a5a38fc0e\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_ae918be444c84d12609b2e1df09af50c\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2432,1,NULL,2000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Rush issued this certificate documenting that Samuel Cole attended 3 courses of his lectures on Chemistry and Pharmacy. Signed by Rush, Professor of Chemistry, College of Philadelphia.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"a82ec4ad2fb26c9b36023b673a4de257\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_dd7e10bbb149eff4a161f74c2d7e6006\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2433,1,NULL,2000,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"36d75399bc06aedc4fddf453ffe7d1e4\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_ebd57b1c987efd5bf0c0da54da1ac1f7\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2434,1,NULL,2001,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Sworn statement that the certificate dated 1 July 1784, payable to Thomas Gilby and signed by John Pierce, is really the property of Dickinson College. signed by Benjamin Rush.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"c948344ea16fd92732facf65b6690949\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_cce3735ea7370e99d76bc8ad31484098\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2435,1,NULL,2001,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"f4beb99fa969be2f9c6b74bad56f1e3a\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_d8e2c547e3912dff90f611f9e48de10e\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2436,1,NULL,2002,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Land deed for the Williamsburg tract purchased by Benjamin Rush, signed by Gov. Thomas Mifflin and Dep. Sec. James Trimble, with the Pennsylvania State seal, with notice that it was recorded in the state patent books.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"791e6a08c5bd33a22ecddfccb8752d36\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_787c511570976ccb538ea8cdd3bdac7e\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2437,1,NULL,2002,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"77f3e267854b4f6ba60aa83366139021\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_171ae2f7a5afc69c49588fedc9a91d0c\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56','2019-09-25 01:14:56',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2438,1,22,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_3fbc83697b6a5a62d0eb0f3a669ea271\",\"type\":\"abstract\",\"content\":[\"The Benjamin and Julia Stockton Rush papers include letters, writings, financial records, a few legal documents and one educational record. Benjamin Rush\'s personal and professional outgoing letters, with some incoming letters, cover a wide variety of topics, but focus primarily on medical concerns, particularly the 1793 and other yellow fever epidemics in Philadelphia, as well as mental illness and its treatment, and the medical department of the Continental Army. There are a few letters from others to Julia Stockton Rush that seek to continue ties with her and the Rush family or offer condolences following Benjamin\'s death. Collection also contains a medical case book and a fragment of an essay or lecture written by Benjamin Rush, along with his travel diary for a trip to meet with the Board of Trustees for Dickinson College in 178[4]; other writings include Julia Rush\'s devotional journal and exercise book. The financial records include a few statements and receipts, but primarily contain two account books, one maintained by Benjamin Rush, the other by Rush with his wife. These account books provide a complete picture of the family finances from the period before the couple married, almost to Julia\'s death. Legal documents include a sworn statement and a land patent, and there is an educational record for one of Rush\'s students.\"]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2439,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_langmaterial\",\"persistent_id\":\"e376ca67ef9c89a8720525e95b7149cd\",\"type\":\"langmaterial\",\"content\":[\"English\"]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,66,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2440,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_langmaterial\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_ff8d82cbff853d3dd45eaa999e61cb9e\",\"type\":\"langmaterial\",\"content\":[\"Materials are in English.\"]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,67,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2441,1,22,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_325ad864e3e98726708a34b440f3d4bb\",\"label\":\"Conditions Governing Access\",\"type\":\"accessrestrict\",\"rights_restriction\":{\"local_access_restriction_type\":[]},\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Collection is open for research.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"0021927446ccfd995bb66fd1f40ce97e\"}]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2442,1,22,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_bdc3743e0b3cf367e34f4071d09177fa\",\"label\":\"Arrangement\",\"type\":\"arrangement\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Arranged into the following series: Letters, Writings, Financial Records, and Legal Documents and Educational Records.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"5afb68591ecc92a947ffb514eb35fdfc\"}]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2443,1,22,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_a23b742e2c36fd5adc4e0e22e73fde2a\",\"label\":\"Biographical Note\",\"type\":\"bioghist\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Benjamin Rush was a physician, politician, social reformer, educator and humanitarian, as well as the founder of Dickinson College in Carlisle, Pennsylvania. He married Julia Stockton in 1776.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"08dd7b5f4c9cd105f8fd8184405a2d6a\"},{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_chronology\",\"title\":\"Benjamin Rush\",\"publish\":true,\"items\":[{\"event_date\":\"1746 January 4\",\"events\":[\"Born, in Byberry Township, Pa.\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1760\",\"events\":[\"Graduated with A. B., College of New Jersey (Princeton)\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1761-1766\",\"events\":[\"Medical apprenticeship, College of Philadelphia medical department\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1768\",\"events\":[\"Completed medical degree, University of Edinburgh\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1769\",\"events\":[\"Began medical practice in Philadelphia\",\"Appointed Professor of Chemistry in College of Philadelphia\'s medical department\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1776\",\"events\":[\"Took his seat in Second Continental Congress\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1776 August 2\",\"events\":[\"Signed Declaration of Independence\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1777 April\",\"events\":[\"Commissioned Surgeon General of Middle Department of the Continental Army\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1778\",\"events\":[\"Resigned from the Army\",\"Became lecturer at University of the State of Pennsylvania\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1783\",\"events\":[\"Helped found Dickinson College in Carlisle, Pa.\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1784-1813\",\"events\":[\"Surgeon at Pennsylvania Hospital, with responsibility for psychiatric ward\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1797-1813\",\"events\":[\"Treasurer of the U.S. Mint\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1813\",\"events\":[\"Died\"]}],\"subnote_guid\":\"0058ad6e0093302e1948c50c640307bc\"},{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_chronology\",\"title\":\"Julia Stockton Rush\",\"publish\":true,\"items\":[{\"event_date\":\"1759\",\"events\":[\"Born, at \\\"Morven\\\" family estate near Princeton, N.J.\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1776\",\"events\":[\"Married Benjamin Rush; the couple went on to have 13 children\"]},{\"event_date\":\"1848\",\"events\":[\"Died at their county property, \\\"Sydenham\\\" (now 15th Street and Columbus Ave, Philadelphia)\"]}],\"subnote_guid\":\"aa08773f6e15a009b8760bc4028aab56\"}]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2444,1,22,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_54177c4564559ff95b8c44280a26160e\",\"label\":\"Preferred Citation\",\"type\":\"prefercite\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"[Identification of item], Benjamin and Julia Stockton Rush papers, 1766-1845 and undated, David M. Rubenstein Rare Book &amp; Manuscript Library, Duke University.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"60bbff29b40602db8b445480b0ab7805\"}]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2445,1,22,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_9ef542b2adc6a537120f8489a96022f2\",\"label\":\"Related Materials\",\"type\":\"relatedmaterial\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Sarah Eve diary, 1772-1773. Eve was the daughter of ship captain and merchant Oswell Eve, and the fiancee of Benjamin Rush until her death on 4 Dec. 1774, three weeks before the date set for their marriage.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"664c6354222dfe08626570d9d2dac17d\"}]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2446,1,22,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_085914a72deaeeff2fd3d690ba01a201\",\"label\":\"Collection Overview\",\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The Benjamin and Julia Stockton Rush papers include letters, writings, financial records, a few legal documents and one educational record. \\n\\n Benjamin Rush\'s personal and professional outgoing letters, with some incoming letters, cover a wide variety of topics, but focus primarily on medical concerns, particularly the 1793 and other yellow fever epidemics in Philadelphia, as well as mental illness and its treatment, and the medical department of the Continental Army. \\n\\n There are a few letters from others to Julia Stockton Rush that seek to continue ties with her and the Rush family or offer condolences following Benjamin\'s death. Collection also contains a medical case book and a fragment of an essay or lecture written by Benjamin Rush, along with his travel diary for a trip to meet with the Board of Trustees for Dickinson College in 178[4]; other writings include Julia Rush\'s devotional journal and exercise book. \\n\\n The financial records include a few statements and receipts, but primarily contain two account books, one maintained by Benjamin Rush, the other by Rush with his wife. These account books provide a complete picture of the family finances from the period before the couple married, almost to Julia\'s death. \\n\\n Legal documents include a sworn statement and a land patent, and there is an educational record for one of Rush\'s students.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"97a88efcbbe75e87f8ec5ce1610b8451\"}]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2447,1,22,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_2a0d85afea56333f3735a15091ac11e6\",\"label\":\"Conditions Governing Use\",\"type\":\"userestrict\",\"rights_restriction\":{\"local_access_restriction_type\":[]},\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The copyright interests in this collection have not been transferred to Duke University. For more information, consult the copyright section of the Regulations and Procedures of the David M. Rubenstein Rare Book &amp; Manuscript Library.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"5f708d52801772d56a0e3509c58a3519\"}]}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04','2019-09-25 02:02:04',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2448,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1