des a separate invitation for Rush to dine with the ?Washington.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"1e9add5bd8d928901111ccaa51f59bc0\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_6f19242e08f603bc9ac4d5917f6b5631\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2923,1,NULL,2142,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"3 pages; 23 cm\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_46a64524b4565268139df7dad0940435\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2924,1,NULL,2142,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"e3225d933e294cff8440b58caae4a397\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_3ac1f0680fa5519cb0fd6a08f3d49bf1\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2925,1,NULL,2142,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Wayne describes his fever and consumption and their treatment, following his loss of blood \\\"in defence of the rights &amp; liberties of America, \'from her coldest, to her hottest sun.\'\\\"\",\"subnote_guid\":\"9f5eaefa75c81fec3bd517212aa3cda2\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_5a782a343b23db2212002a9f6e60fa74\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2926,1,NULL,2143,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"23 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_a45a4c59ffb453d5f2b58b6d837abb73\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2927,1,NULL,2143,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The diary records Rush\'s travel, accompanied by a servant and via horses, between the outskirts of Philadelphia and Carlisle, Pennsylvania, for an initial meeting with the trustees of Dickinson College. During the meeting the Trustees selected Dr. Charles Nisbet to serve as the College\'s first president. Rush described the taverns and other travel lodges at which he stopped, along with Tavern staff and other patrons, the quality of the food and drink, along with conversations he witnessed or took part in. Discussion often centered on the topics of the Constitution, paper money, as well as Dickinson College. Rush also described the results of a rapid Spring thaw on the Susquehanna River, the unusually cold weather, the scenery, and the presence whiskey stills in Irish settlements and their impact on their communities.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"18743ede0703d15c6b379837e689a581\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_16c9784312f30f9a01441146f64f7f99\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2928,1,NULL,2143,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"accecae97aaaf7bc971898ad05995303\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_0fc510c13bbab565bec03a2a58c2e0e1\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2929,1,NULL,2143,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"5-page transcription available\",\"subnote_guid\":\"54759ab10265ebef9871366142fb0a72\"}],\"type\":\"altformavail\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_78e9daaa7019023fc12e43a8f17dbb3a\",\"label\":\"Existence and Location of Copies\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2930,1,NULL,2144,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"74 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_c76be363ccb3bd16799674e3906634b4\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2931,1,NULL,2144,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"8ff57b9559382652958a48c46b541cf8\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_072b51eae28123e8565932f6e1e096c5\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2932,1,NULL,2144,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"In the casebook, Rush provided brief histories for his treatment of about 75 individuals. Entries generally included the year, patient\'s name, presented medical issue, dates of treatment, prescriptions applied, pulses noted, and the progression or resolution of the problem. Rheumatism was the most common complaint, along with dropsy (edema), pneumonia, diarrhea, and mania. Among the other illnesses listed were palsy (paralysis), fever, typhus, epilepsy, consumption, scurvy, hydrothorax, swelled spleen, and hysteria.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"275cb2547271757b20a0d33250bf8529\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_9e36419b9eff8c519091709a75f0febb\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2933,1,NULL,2145,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"222 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_fef8d7befb873261a81c3548298b871e\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2934,1,NULL,2145,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Rush not only detailed her religious thoughts and practiced devotional exercises but also outlined her feelings regarding family matters, especially in regard to her bereavement following her husband\'s death. She requested intersession for family members, such as when her daughters emigrated to England and Canada and their later return, when they suffered serious illnesses, and blessings for the christenings of her grandchildren. She also noted her general physical and mental health as she aged. Entries are irregular, but often annually mark the New Year and her birthday on March 2nd.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"943078540c74cb8b101897c404a211a6\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_111b12b49443e042ddd5fa9356ea43e6\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2935,1,NULL,2145,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"c866e26f60f8ae3532bc88130a19e63d\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_ccc184c780ae0c4a95f76f91fa7a9fbc\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47','2019-09-25 13:18:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2936,1,NULL,2146,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"2-page transcription available.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"d3742550d1c58c237bb75d242c72da8e\"}],\"type\":\"altformavail\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_b16bbaf275e2a4346ab7ba9286497c06\",\"label\":\"Existence and Location of Copies\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2937,1,NULL,2146,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Lecture or essay regarding use of cordial remedies and bleeding, a discussion of influenza, along with a 2-page partial report on an autopsy that noted the presence of a tumor in the abdomen.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"cfe0f629f2a83f3e591a611f0543e8ac\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_f2abec9d0f2042719b76e7eb7e55c419\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2938,1,NULL,2146,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"6101ba2239577ea8f6114c964e2aa8dd\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_2bf589605f06c5c978dd687c07232296\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2939,1,NULL,2147,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Presentation note for three unnamed items initialed by Richard Rush, son of Bejamin and Julia Stockton Rush.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"c30dc2693a337e6eb380592b63b0bfd6\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_0053dfed5bc13ffeee4c14ac6414fd5f\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2940,1,NULL,2147,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"63e2b8429a85034889dcaf9f4e68ea2c\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_0358b21ecdc3d38c16528900f8dae910\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2941,1,NULL,2148,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Includes statements and receipts for medicines, advice, consultations, and sundries. In one case, Rush collected a fee on behalf of another physician. Julia Stockton Rush also served as collector, along with her husband. Includes a receipt from Richard Henderson in Leesburg, Va., for payment on the account of Mr. Carter, who had been a patient in Rush\'s care (see Letters series).\",\"subnote_guid\":\"b94c506941b31ff143b4c4b7d99b4a04\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_2d5e8a4ed5c22211fde63c52e773df7f\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2942,1,NULL,2148,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"b189983fb8e86779f7bfb98f50b3563a\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_2606f259f35e550d36ee47f534643164\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2943,1,NULL,2149,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"259 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_b94a693ec6dd9288b3fc30089d0486b1\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2944,1,NULL,2149,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Contains primarily Benjamin Rush\'s records of his expenses, including tax and bond payments, rental property fees, classes and dance lessons for family members, as well as money lent or advanced, accounts paid, cash received, and income from boarders. Rush noted the wide variety of areas where his money was spent, from postage and travel, to clothing and shoes, to household provisions and stores, along with medicines purchased. In addition, Rush created accounts for servants when they arrived, and noted their wages and any increased wages, advances, or loans; cloth, clothing, and shoes provided; with occasional notes on their personal and work habits and work history, and when they exited his service or married. Several of the comments have been redacted, along with a few pages of the account book. Finally, Rush made a few brief commonplace notes randomly in the volume, providing a \\\"style sheet\\\" for description of pulses, outlining a few prescriptions for patients, describing the weather, listing inventories of his furniture and linens, recording a few recipes, and in 1783, noting the news of possible peace with England.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"a4ab2201dd170df9ab83225f9cab7bcd\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_fab942e5a8250b77ef1823c9ee7ddf86\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2945,1,NULL,2149,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"844a8dbb0eeaab33686bf22ee6a05a0f\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_fff7d43fbae42c1db84c25ecdf5c4e72\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2946,1,NULL,2150,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_singlepart\",\"content\":[\"146 pages\"],\"type\":\"physdesc\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_68ec4e660c6cfe98eddce4bb9aee7dcb\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2947,1,NULL,2150,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Contains primarily accounts for individuals the Rush\'s employed in their household, including various house servants, cooks, coachmen, farmers and gardeners, along with accounts for work completed by washerwomen outside the residence. Individual accounts include the servant\'s name, followed by notes on pay and payments made, as well as any holds on pay, advances, loans, and pay rate increases. They also indicated when an individual was supplied with shoes or clothing, or had time off to visit the country. In addition, for the majority of the individuals, Benjamin continued his habit of adding a descriptive note when the person left their service, stating the reason for the departure, commenting on the quality of that servant\'s work, outlining their personal and work habits (especially their drinking habits), whether they married or not, and their race or ethnic background. Includes an incomplete alphabetical index for servant names. There are a few additional household accounts briefly noted, for wood and an umbrella, as well as two receipts, one for taxes and another (laid-in) for bread.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"d20fa988ba283f5f23e6a5bd43c983c6\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_5c96ad6ec2fa68e3ea1b4d4890d74a1d\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2948,1,NULL,2150,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"645d57485f078573de18fe8880e58de6\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_ae918be444c84d12609b2e1df09af50c\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2949,1,NULL,2151,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Rush issued this certificate documenting that Samuel Cole attended 3 courses of his lectures on Chemistry and Pharmacy. Signed by Rush, Professor of Chemistry, College of Philadelphia.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"b9a9f822ec76d78654c34cc35f8abf4e\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_dd7e10bbb149eff4a161f74c2d7e6006\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2950,1,NULL,2151,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"8dd49de5885ba93b1f0385b14ebd3e94\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_ebd57b1c987efd5bf0c0da54da1ac1f7\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2951,1,NULL,2152,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Sworn statement that the certificate dated 1 July 1784, payable to Thomas Gilby and signed by John Pierce, is really the property of Dickinson College. signed by Benjamin Rush.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"4bb55660e1aaab9e6110a274fbd16dd8\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_cce3735ea7370e99d76bc8ad31484098\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2952,1,NULL,2152,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"96f73eadab8f6e4b20425698a94bb06d\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_d8e2c547e3912dff90f611f9e48de10e\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2953,1,NULL,2153,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Land deed for the Williamsburg tract purchased by Benjamin Rush, signed by Gov. Thomas Mifflin and Dep. Sec. James Trimble, with the Pennsylvania State seal, with notice that it was recorded in the state patent books.\",\"subnote_guid\":\"d2e30c67d50a0c7515524dfe9961a828\"}],\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_787c511570976ccb538ea8cdd3bdac7e\",\"label\":\"Scope and Contents\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2954,1,NULL,2153,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"subnotes\":[{\"publish\":true,\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Gift of Josiah Charles Trent Collection, 1956\",\"subnote_guid\":\"27092fdfa1d10cf8de5acad52a5b33bc\"}],\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_171ae2f7a5afc69c49588fedc9a91d0c\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\"}','noahh','noahh','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48','2019-09-25 13:18:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2955,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_langmaterial\",\"persistent_id\":\"c1bb0bf272d67c61f98627a51b001acb\",\"type\":\"langmaterial\",\"content\":[\"English\"]}','jodiab','jodiab','2019-09-27 21:20:47','2019-09-27 21:20:47','2019-09-27 21:20:47',NULL,NULL,70,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2956,1,8,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_d9b74d20f50ddfff1f4b24b45ce0fc0d\",\"label\":\"Content Description\",\"type\":\"scopecontent\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Records include administrative and governance materials, publications, and memorabilia. Patricularly noteworthy is correspondence with Senator John F. Kennedy regarding his visit to Carpe Diem University to give a speech and the Fence Club dinner he attended while on campus. Kennedy had connections to the Fence Club through friends from Choate Rosemary Hall who attended Carpe Diem.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"342b15f63bfaf6b1163f5b5d019e16c9\"}]}','jodiab','jodiab','2019-09-27 21:20:47','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:47',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2957,1,8,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_0af8c91d2b6618148f9a0d34031dbf93\",\"label\":\"Biographical / Historical\",\"type\":\"bioghist\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The Fence Club at Carpe Diem University has a venerable history, evolving from a 19th-century quasi-secret society for men to a service organization known and respected throughout the City on a Hill community. The origins of the Fence Club are murky, as it emerged as a secretive society in the early 1880s when Carpe Diem was an all-male college. It takes its name from the fence that separated the main Carpe Diem quadrangle from City on a Hill Park, which is adjacent to the campus. Legend has it that juniors would congregate on a Spring evening on the fence, and some would be secretly signalled to come to a specific location to receive an invitation to join the Fence Club.\\n\\n Following the end of World War I, the club emerged as a more visible presence on the Carpe Diem campus, serving as a social nexus for seniors who were invited to be members and a center around which charitable activities to benefit the City on a Hill community were organized. Fence Club members are members for life, and the organization, incorporated in 1899 independently from Carpe Diem University, has amassed a considerable amount of money over the years through donations and bequests from its members.\\n\\nIn 1925 the club purchased an ornate mansion on Regal Street, near the campus, which continues to serve as the center of Fence Club activities to this day. The Fence Club began inviting women students as members in 1967, the year after Carpe Diem University became coeducational. Potential members are still recruited in a secretive ritual on a set day each Spring, and only rising seniors may be invited to membership. Twenty-three new members are initiated each year, as they have been since its first recorded initiation, in honor of the founding of Carpe Diem in 1823.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"e9652ac18eb4b3e2fdf8bbb2b6bebd1a\"}]}','jodiab','jodiab','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2958,1,8,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_f5e87094e1c4ada9ea0efae3452e1e9b\",\"label\":\"Immediate Source of Acquisition\",\"type\":\"acqinfo\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The records were donated to Your Name Here Special Collections in 1987 by the then governing council of the Fence Club, through the person of then president Sandra Dacsandra.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"f3c753dfadb2095f7000599182a6fd59\"}]}','jodiab','jodiab','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2959,1,8,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_c89ef6839fcbfeb9533a6cd9aabf444c\",\"label\":\"Arrangement\",\"type\":\"arrangement\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"The records are arranged alphabetically by type of material. This arrangement was imposed by YNHSC staff during processing, based on the as-received order of a large part of the material.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"6e2e45be11d1a59b597a09b4ab565bb5\"}]}','jodiab','jodiab','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2960,1,8,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_70d1b9d5370ce602a51ee4e23978ce1e\",\"label\":\"Accruals\",\"type\":\"accruals\",\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"More recent records are retained by the Fence Club and may be donated to YNHSC at some future date.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"e6a7a05fbf714a83d2307440341b8b0f\"}]}','jodiab','jodiab','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2961,1,8,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_dfdef5498dada05734c031cbe11bc76d\",\"label\":\"Conditions Governing Access\",\"type\":\"accessrestrict\",\"rights_restriction\":{\"local_access_restriction_type\":[]},\"subnotes\":[{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_text\",\"content\":\"Written permission of the current president of the Fence Club is required in order to access the records. Contact the repository for details on obtaining access permission.\",\"publish\":true,\"subnote_guid\":\"b2a159ef6c0a3b68c2c8dc713293d694\"}]}','jodiab','jodiab','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48','2019-09-27 21:20:48',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2962,1,8,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,1,_binary '{\"jsonmodel_type\":\"note_multipart\",\"persistent_id\":\"aspace_96ca223af487f9f95a417a68b513ed28